49:# At slice checkpoints, run G1 (`bb test:sub <own>`). Before landing a slice, run
50:# G2 (`bb test:changed` in the worktree across all three lanes).
51:# Full repo-wide `bb test` (G3) is the mandatory landing gate on master after merge.
53:# for every gate from G1 upward. Run one lane set at a time per machine to avoid
126:1. **G0 Iterate**: Run only the subsystem's JVM lane (`bb test:sub:clj <own>` or `clojure -M:test -n <ns>`).
127:2. **G1 Checkpoint**: Run the three-lane subsystem test (`bb test:sub <own>`). Proves the home suite across all three hosts before reporting ready.
128:3. **G2 Land**: Run `bb test:changed` in the worktree across all three lanes (plus `bb test:sub <own> --slow` if slow tests are present). Covers dependents across the change (for foundation subsystems like `dao.stream` or `dao.jing`, this correctly runs nearly the full suite).
129:4. **G3 Master**: The mandatory landing gate on master after merge, and for any wide change (`bb test`).
130:5. **G4 Release**: Full or slow test run before a big release or cross-cutting merge (`bb test:slow` or `bb test:all`), and at each phase boundary of a multi-phase track (owner decision 2026-10-12; see "Test tiers: quick and slow" below). G0 to G3 run the quick tier; G4 runs the slow tier.
203:- **Cadence:** the quick tier at every checkpoint (G1) and landing (G2, G3); the slow
205:  (the existing G4). There is no nightly run.
